menu "EspMeshCompact"

    config MTCOMPACT_TEXT_COMPRESSION
        bool "Enable Unishox2 compression for outgoing text"
        default n
        help
            Allows MtCompact::setTextCompression(true) to send
            TEXT_MESSAGE_COMPRESSED_APP when the compressed form is shorter.

            This is off by default because the Unishox2 compressor costs about
            4.2 kB of flash, and unlike the decompressor -- which is always
            built, so incoming compressed text is always understood -- nothing
            needs it unless this node chooses to compress what it sends.

            Turning this on without also calling setTextCompression(true)
            changes nothing except the binary size.

endmenu
